# The site works without any environment variables for public content: the platform address and organisation slug are
# built in (lib/site.ts, PLATFORM). Set the NEXT_PUBLIC_* values only to point at another API, e.g. staging.
# WARNING: anything named NEXT_PUBLIC_* is copied into the browser bundle. Never put a secret in one.

# --- Public (safe for the browser) ---
# API origin of the counsellor platform (NO /api/v1 at the end).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL=https://apicounsellor.jdinfotechsolutions.in
# Organisation slug of the FastAdmission tenant (tenant ID 00001) in the platform.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TENANT_SLUG=fastadmission
# Admin console (opened from /admin/leads)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ADMIN_URL=https://counsellor.jdinfotechsolutions.in

# --- Server-only secrets (set in the hosting dashboard; never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_) ---
# Per-organisation secret key for the platform's inbound lead webhook (POST <API>/public/leads/webhook/<slug>).
# Enquiry forms post to this site's /api/leads route, which adds the
# ---- Lead intake (SERVER-ONLY, never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_) ----
# All enquiry forms post to this site's own /api/leads route, which forwards to <API>/public/leads/webhook/<slug>.
# When the platform requires a per-organisation secret on that webhook, set it here (copy it from the admin). It is added on the
# server and never sent to the browser. Leave empty while the platform webhook is still open.
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Header the platform expects the secret in (default x-webhook-secret).
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_SECRET_HEADER=x-webhook-secret
